// MOTION CONSTANTS - where the game's own cast animations put the emitter, and how it gets there.
//
// GENERATED by tools/k19a_motion_stats.mjs from 234 authored casts of 135 models:
// 139 SPELL casts (clip 9/11/13, the ones this file's MOTION tables aggregate) and 85 clip-5
// throws (MOTION_THROW). AGGREGATES ONLY: no model id, name or disc geometry is in this file. The
// per-row measurements live in /home/dorij/scratch-research/anatomy/motion-stats.json.
//
// How to read it: every measure is a distribution { p10, p50, p90 } over the casts of that class.
//   hH  emitter height above the model's own floor,    as a share of BODY HEIGHT
//   fH  forward offset from the torso bone's point,    as a share of BODY HEIGHT (+z forward)
//   lH  |lateral| distance from the torso bone's point, as a share of BODY HEIGHT (unsigned: the
//       solver picks the side, so the pooled class records the distance from the midline)
//   hL fL lL  the same as a share of ARM LENGTH, measured FROM THE SHOULDER (an arm length has a
//       shoulder origin, not a floor one) - arm emitters only
//   handHH handFH handLH  the WRIST point (the hand the solver must place), body shares
//   handHL handFL  the same in arm lengths
//   backH upH  the wind-up: how far the emitter draws BEHIND and ABOVE its release point, body shares
//   backL upL  the same in arm lengths
//   travelH    the largest distance the emitter travels from its release point during the wind-up
//   speedH     forward speed through the release frame (mean of the last 5 ticks), body heights/tick
//   peakSpeedH the fastest forward step anywhere in the wind-up
//   windup flight follow total  phase durations in ticks (bind -> release -> strike -> end)
//   peakBefore how many ticks before release the wind-up peak is
//   strikeHH strikeFH  the emitter's height/forward at the STRIKE (follow-through)
//   handGapH   distance between the two hands at release (arm bodies only)
//   backShare upShare  share of the class that moves back / up by at least 0.05 H during the cast
//
// "eyes" has no spell cast in the corpus (2 clip-5 throws only): it is a head-front emitter, so
// motionFor() resolves an eye emitter to the mouth record instead of returning null.
//
// 233 of the 234 scripts author an op10 99 strike; the rest have no strike phase.
// 6 scripts fire before their own body starts and 4 points are mis-measured props:
// both are excluded from these aggregates (flagged in rows[] of the JSON).
